and output lines.\n\n**One structural change:** the placeholder numbering had C/Py/Java before cmds. I renumbered (`git mv`) to match your stated order — `02_install_cmds`, `03_install_c`, `04_install_py`, `05_install_java`.\n\n## Verified\n- 71/71 internal links resolve (`tools/check_links.sh`, also wired into CI)\n- all 6 scripts pass `bash -n`; bootstrap tested — sourcing `common.sh` works from any cwd, and the platform guard fires correctly on macOS\n- 13/13 code blocks got labels and copy buttons; copy output confirmed paste-ready; no horizontal overflow; dark mode confirmed\n\n## Not verified\n`shellcheck` isn't installed here and Docker isn't running, so **the scripts have not actually been executed on Ubuntu** — only parsed and read. CI (`.github/workflows/shellcheck.yml`) will run shellcheck, PSScriptAnalyzer, and the link check on first push.\n\nTwo things I can do next if you want: `brew install shellcheck` to lint locally now, or start Docker and do a real end-to-end run in `ubuntu:24.04`. Nothing is committed yet.","type":"text"}]}
