{"v":1,"agent":"claude-code","cli_version":"0.9.0","type":"assistant","ts":"2026-08-05T09:25:34.711Z","id":"msg_011CdjMtKTMPGqvJYpSrtS3c","input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":769,"content":[{"text":"Done. Step 2's `jq` section is now a beginner-level validity check, and the deeper material lives in a new step 10.\n\n## Step 2 — \"Checking a JSON file with jq\"\n\nTeaches one idea: **output means valid, an error means broken.**\n\n- What JSON is — key/value pairs, in plain language\n- Your four-key file: `name`, `roll_number`, `image_url`, `sankalpam`\n- Create it with `nano` (including which keys save and exit — they've never used an editor)\n- `jq . student.json` → prints it back = valid\n- Break it on purpose, see the error, fix it\n\nNo pipes, no `select`, no `-r`, no filters, no API calls.\n\n## I had to correct my own page\n\nI'd written a plausible-*looking* error message rather than a real one. Actual output, verified:\n\n| Mistake | What jq really prints |\n|---|---|\n| Missing comma | `Expected separator between values at line 4, column 13` |\n| Trailing comma | `Expected another key-value pair` |\n| Unquoted key | `Invalid numeric literal` |\n\nTesting also surfaced something genuinely useful for beginners: **the reported line is one past the mistake.** Delete the comma on line 3 and jq blames line 4 — it only notices when it reaches the next value. That's now a callout, since a first-timer staring at a line that looks fine is exactly where they'd get stuck. I also noted that `Invalid numeric literal` is a strange way to say \"this key needs quotes\".\n\n## Step 10 — \"Doing more with jq\"\n\nPractice page, no installer — jq already came with step 2. Contains everything moved out: `.field` access, `-r`, multi-field extraction, the `readings.json` list exercises (now a table with expected answers), the GitHub API examples, and a cheat sheet. Plus an explanation of why tasks 4–6 need `[ ]`, which was the unstated trap in the original.\n\n`docs/examples/student.json` added. 141/141 links resolve, shellcheck clean.\n\nDocker Desktop has stopped, so I verified the jq behaviour with local jq 1.7.1 rather than Ubuntu's 1.7 — the parse messages are from the same jq release line, but if you want it confirmed on Ubuntu exactly, I can restart Docker.\n\nReady for your next set of changes.","type":"text"}]}
