03c/span\u003eping -c 4 github.com\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/div\u003e\n\n  \u003ch3\u003eFetch a web page\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n  \u003cp\u003eDownload a page and print it straight to the screen.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n  \u003cdiv class=\"codeblock\" data-label=\"ubuntu terminal\"\u003e\n\u003cpre\u003e\u003ccode\u003e\u003cspan class=\"prompt\"\u003e$ \u003c/span\u003ecurl -s https://example.com\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/div\u003e\n\n  \u003ch3\u003eRead something long, one screen at a time\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n  \u003cp\u003e\n    The same page, but paged. Press \u003ckbd\u003eSpace\u003c/kbd\u003e for the next screen and\n    \u003ckbd\u003eq\u003c/kbd\u003e to quit.\n  \u003c/p\u003e\n\n  \u003cdiv class=\"codeblock\" data-label=\"ubuntu terminal\"\u003e\n\u003cpre\u003e\u003ccode\u003e\u003cspan class=\"prompt\"\u003e$ \u003c/span\u003ecurl -s https://example.com | less\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/div\u003e\n\n  \u003cdiv class=\"callout warn\"\u003e\n    \u003cdiv class=\"callout-title\"\u003eStuck on a screen with no prompt?\u003c/div\u003e\n    \u003cp\u003e\n      You are inside \u003ccode\u003eless\u003c/code\u003e. Press \u003ckbd\u003eq\u003c/kbd\u003e to come back to the\n      terminal. This catches everyone once.\n    \u003c/p\u003e\n  \u003c/div\u003e\n\n  \u003ch3\u003eAsk what a file really is\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n  \u003cp\u003e\n    File names can say anything. \u003ccode\u003efile\u003c/code\u003e looks inside and tells you\n    what it actually found.\n  \u003c/p\u003e\n\n  \u003cdiv class=\"codeblock\" data-label=\"ubuntu terminal\"\u003e\n\u003cpre\u003e\u003ccode\u003e\u003cspan class=\"prompt\"\u003e$ \u003c/span\u003efile /bin/ls\n\u003cspan class=\"out\"\u003e/bin/ls: ELF 64-bit LSB pie executable, x86-64, dynamically linked\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/div\u003e\n\n  \u003ch3\u003eSee a folder as a tree\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n  \u003cp\u003e\n    Show what is in the current fold