{"v":1,"agent":"claude-code","cli_version":"0.9.0","type":"assistant","ts":"2026-08-05T10:03:19.481Z","id":"msg_011CdjQmRB3hYTbnJMxeyAfG","input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":877,"content":[{"text":"Step 1 now pins Ubuntu 24.04 LTS.\n\n## The script\n\n```powershell\n$distro = if ($env:WSL_DISTRO) { $env:WSL_DISTRO } else { 'Ubuntu-24.04' }\n```\n\n**A second bug came with this change.** The already-installed check was:\n\n```powershell\n$alreadyThere = $installed | Where-Object { $_ -like 'Ubuntu*' }\n```\n\nThat wildcard matches *any* Ubuntu. On a machine with Ubuntu-22.04 already present, it would have reported \"already installed\" and skipped 24.04 entirely — pinning the version in one place while silently not installing it. Now an exact `-eq $distro` match, and if another Ubuntu is found it says so and installs 24.04 alongside:\n\n```\nwarn Found other Ubuntu versions: Ubuntu-22.04\nwarn Installing Ubuntu-24.04 alongside them. They can coexist.\n```\n\n`wsl --set-default Ubuntu-24.04` now runs unconditionally, so a bare `wsl` opens the right one. The failure path points at `Ubuntu-24.04` in `wsl --list --online` rather than a generic name.\n\n## Docs\n\n- Callout explaining **why** pinned: `-d Ubuntu` tracks Microsoft's current default and drifts, so two people months apart get different systems. Also spells out what LTS means.\n- Start-menu entry corrected to **\"Ubuntu 24.04.x LTS\"** — it isn't called plain \"Ubuntu\" anymore.\n- Windows path corrected to `\\\\wsl$\\Ubuntu-24.04\\home\\yourname`.\n- Verification section now says to look for `Ubuntu-24.04` with `*` in `wsl --list --verbose`, and `wsl --set-version Ubuntu-24.04 2` is its own copy box.\n- Manual fallback uses `-d Ubuntu-24.04`.\n- `WSL_DISTRO` default updated in the scripts reference; README and landing card mention 24.04.\n- CLAUDE.md records the pin and warns that moving it means re-testing every step — package names do shift between releases, which already bit this project twice (`xxd`/`vim-common`, `bsdextrautils`/`bsdmainutils`).\n\n141/141 links resolve.\n\nTwo open items from before I paused: making **step 3 beginner-friendly** (you interrupted while I was capturing a real lldb session for accurate output), and I still haven't executed this PowerShell script — it needs real Windows, so it remains reviewed and linted only. Want me to pick step 3 back up?","type":"text"}]}
